-- Spot checks of the index, each expected value read by hand from the text file.
-- Line 55: the heading printed for section 5.
#ASSERT `the heading of the provision with the identifier` "s 5" EQUALS JUST "Calculation of value of fee and penalty units"
-- A subsection carries the heading of its section: line 58 is section 5(3).
#ASSERT `the heading of the provision with the identifier` "s 5(3)" EQUALS JUST "Calculation of value of fee and penalty units"
-- Line 82: section 8(1A) is printed under the heading of section 8 (line 78).
#ASSERT `the heading of the provision with the identifier` "s 8(1A)" EQUALS JUST "Certain monetary amounts to be construed in fee units or penalty units"
-- Line 97: a subparagraph of section 9(2)(a).
#ASSERT `the heading of the provision with the identifier` "s 9(2)(a)(ii)" EQUALS JUST "Regulations"
-- Line 118: the heading of section 11 as printed, with its en dash.
#ASSERT `the heading of the provision with the identifier` "s 11" EQUALS JUST "Provisions for 2012–2013"
-- A defined term of section 3 (line 47).
#ASSERT `the identifier is in the index` "s 3 'penalty'"
-- The text has no section 13 in this range and no section 5(9).
#ASSERT NOT `the identifier is in the index` "s 13"
#ASSERT NOT `the identifier is in the index` "s 5(9)"
